---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Money: Crypto Near MBR City"
  description="Where MBR City residents actually handle crypto — nearby exchange options and how buying district property with crypto works in practice."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Money</p>
    <h1>Crypto, close to the district</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      MBR City's central location — bordering Business Bay and a short
      drive from DIFC and Downtown — means licensed crypto exchange
      infrastructure is close by regardless of which community you're in.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Nearest exchange options</h2>
    <p>
      Licensed exchange desks and ATMs cluster in Business Bay, DIFC, and
      Downtown — a 10–20 minute drive from most MBR City communities, with
      Sobha Hartland typically closest given its Business Bay-adjacent
      location. As with any crypto service, verify current VARA licensing
      directly before using a specific provider.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Buying property with crypto</h2>
    <p>
      Crypto-funded purchases across MBR City's communities generally go
      through a licensed conversion step at the point of transaction rather
      than a developer holding crypto directly — the same mechanics as
      elsewhere in Dubai. Confirm support for this directly with the
      brokerage handling the specific unit before assuming it's available.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Callout>
    DST's crypto vertical covers regulation, exchange options, and the
    buy-with-crypto process network-wide. This page is the MBR City
    summary of that broader coverage.
  </Callout>
</Layout>

